{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773447718,"nonce":"gka8C1pfwUJ+FRfL6LiWbj2fvSo=","title":"Crash recovery, self-healing, and AI-assisted debug: design + implementation spec","message":"Design spec for making Mandible resilient, self-diagnosing, and optionally self-repairing when it crashes or hangs. Synthesized from independent analyses by Opus and Gemini.\n\n---\n\n## Architecture baseline (what already exists)\n\n- SSE client has exponential backoff reconnect (500ms-15s). Server sends `: heartbeat` every 15s.\n- `RebuildingSplash` overlay already exists, triggered by `mandible:rebuilding` SSE event.\n- `GET /api/health` returns uptime, version, commit hash.\n- `unhandledRejection` is logged but does NOT crash. `uncaughtException` is NOT handled — crash produces no capture.\n- PID file at `~/.cache/mandible/daemon.pid`. Logs at `~/.cache/mandible/launchd-stderr.log` (NDJSON).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Crash Detection: Three Layers\n\nLayer 1 — SSE heartbeat watchdog (UI): track last heartbeat. If no heartbeat for 30s (2 missed beats), enter \"checking\" state. Zero extra traffic.\n\nLayer 2 — Active health poll (triggered by Layer 1): fetch /api/health.\n- 200 OK: SSE reconnect lagging, reset watchdog\n- Network error: daemon down. If mandible:rebuilding was recently received: existing rebuild splash. Otherwise: crash overlay.\n- Timeout (\u003e2s): zombie daemon, show \"Mandible is unresponsive\" variant.\n\nLayer 3 — Server-side crash capture: add uncaughtException handler in src/index.ts (currently missing). Handler writes crash-\u003ctimestamp\u003e.json to ~/.cache/mandible/ and exits with code 2 (distinct from code-1 intentional exits).\n\nOptional: event loop blocking detection (blocked-at or setInterval self-test) for zombie detection before Layer 2 fires.\n\nCrash-loop detection: if crash uptime_seconds \u003c 5 AND multiple crash files within 60s, show \"Mandible is crash-looping\" message with specific recovery advice.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Crash File Schema\n\n{\n  \"timestamp\": \"...\", \"error\": \"...\", \"stack\": \"...\", \"commit\": \"...\",\n  \"uptime_seconds\": 3847, \"memory\": {...}, \"load_avg\": [...],\n  \"recent_logs\": [\"...last 50 NDJSON lines...\"],\n  \"recent_sse_events\": [\"...last 10 SSE event types...\"],\n  \"node_version\": \"...\", \"platform\": \"darwin-arm64\",\n  \"install_mode\": \"dev\", \"exit_code\": 2\n}\n\nNew endpoint: GET /api/system/crash-reports — reads crash-*.json files, served by new daemon after auto-restart.\n\nNever collect: DB contents, env vars, auth command fields, conversation content, absolute paths outside Mandible repo, usernames/hostnames.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Crash Overlay UI\n\nThree buttons in order of prominence:\n1. Restart (primary) — autoStartDaemon(), dismisses on daemon:reloaded event\n2. Debug (secondary, dev-install only) — opens AI debug session in Console tab\n3. Report (tertiary, subtle) — sends crash spec to central server (opt-in)\n\nMulti-tab: BroadcastChannel so only one tab shows Debug; others show \"Debug session opened in another tab.\"\n\n---\n\n## 4. Debug Chat (\"Mandible Resident Surgeon\")\n\nNew endpoint POST /api/system/debug-session:\n1. Reads crash report file\n2. Constructs system prompt (see below)\n3. Writes to temp file\n4. Spawns claude via existing PTY manager in new Console session\n5. Returns session ID so UI navigates to Console tab\n\nSystem prompt includes: crash JSON verbatim, instructions to identify stack frame, check logs, determine root cause, implement fix on feature branch, run build+test, restart to verify. Constraints: never modify main, read CLAUDE.md first.\n\nThe debug chat IS the immediate reward for dev users.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Distribution Model \u0026 Self-Modification\n\ninstallMode() function detects: dev (has .git), npm-global (lib/node_modules/mandible), npm-local, homebrew (/opt/homebrew/), bundled (Tauri).\n\nInstall mode determines: whether Debug appears, whether debug chat has write access, whether fix_proposal is included in phone-home payload.\n\nNon-editable installs (Homebrew, Tauri): do NOT self-modify. Instead:\n- Shadow patch model: support ~/.mandible/patches/ directory. On boot, apply hotfixes in memory via monkeypatching. User can accept a community fix without waiting for new release.\n- npm global: offer \"npm update -g mandible\" if fix version published.\n\nNo forced fork. For dev users: branch+PR via normal auth flow. For package users: patch submission without GitHub account (server-side bot opens PR, user gets attribution).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Phone Home: Privacy-First Crash Spec\n\nStructured spec (NOT raw telemetry):\n- fingerprint (sha256 of stack + commit)\n- mandible_version, mandible_commit, node_version, platform\n- error_type, error_message (truncated 500 chars), stack_trace (relative paths only)\n- crash_phase, uptime_seconds, install_mode\n- fix_proposal (diff if debug chat produced one, opt-in only)\n\nUI shows exact JSON before sending. No account, no form, one click.\n\nServer pipeline:\n1. Deduplicate by fingerprint. Return known status if seen before.\n2. AI triage: code bug with fix / environmental issue / needs more context\n3. If code bug: generate patch, run tests, open PR via bot if tests pass\n4. If environmental: return structured mitigation steps shown in overlay\n5. If unknown: file GitHub issue for manual investigation\n\nPrivacy: HTTPS only, anonymous, opt-in per event, no IP logging beyond request, 90-day retention, \"What gets sent?\" link in overlay.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Motivation Loop\n\nFix first, contribute second.\n\n1. Crash overlay: Restart is the primary action (pain resolved in one click)\n2. \"Check for known fix\" polls central server by fingerprint before asking user to do anything\n3. If known fix: \"A fix was generated 2 hours ago. Apply?\" — instant gratification\n4. If no known fix + dev install: Debug opens AI session that fixes it locally\n5. After local fix: \"Submit this fix so others don't hit it?\" (afterthought, not burden)\n6. After submission: fix notification on next startup when fix is merged\n\nThe community hotfix UX: \"This is a known issue. A fix was generated by another user's agent 2 hours ago. Click here to apply.\"\n\n---\n\n## 8. Edge Cases\n\n- Crash during uncaughtException handler: wrap in try-catch, always exit(2)\n- Crash during auth merge: on restart, scan for executing/approved auth_requests, verify git merge state\n- Multiple browser tabs: BroadcastChannel coordination for debug session\n- SSE reconnect race: dismiss overlay on daemon:reloaded regardless of debug session state\n- DB locked / SQLITE_BUSY cascades: add DB liveness check (SELECT 1) to /api/health response\n- Crash-looping: detect via uptime_seconds \u003c 5 + multiple recent crash files\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Phases\n\nPhase 1 (weekend): uncaughtException handler + crash file, SSE heartbeat watchdog, crash overlay with Restart, /api/system/crash-reports endpoint\n\nPhase 2 (+1 day): /api/system/debug-session, debug chat prompt, wire Debug button to Console\n\nPhase 3 (infrastructure): crash spec submission, central server (Cloudflare Worker + D1), \"Check for known fix\", opt-in setting in Settings UI\n\nPhase 4 (ambitious): server-side AI triage + patch generation, fix notification on startup, shadow patch model, community hotfix UX","files":null}]}